WEBVTT

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.350
Reiji, I'm off to pick up Kousaka.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.720
We'll meet at the park
in front of the arena at 10 o'clock.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.350
Okay, okay.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.320
See ya.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.900
Hey, what are you—

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.770
Whatever, just go already.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.230
Don't order me around!

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.540
You're in my way.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.370
You think you're a knight!?

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.270
Darn kid!

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.980
Just you wait...

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.390
I'm coming full-on.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:59.360
This... is nothing.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.380
Iori, Mr. Ral,
thanks for picking me up.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.820
Thank you for coming over.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.320
You're staying with relatives, right?

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.830
Is it far from here?

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.260
It's about 20 minutes by car.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.130
So I can be there every day
to cheer you on.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.300
That's really nice,
but you don't have to.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.700
You don't want me there?

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.940
What? No!

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.340
It's just I thought there'd be
other places you'd want to go.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.350
Now that you say that...

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.450
No, please wait.
Wait up, Kousaka!

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.250
I feel all itchy.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.860
I somehow feel this itchiness
right down to my bottom.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.730
What's wrong?

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.530
Is it hemorrhoids?

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.200
No it's not!

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.640
Why is Sei so late?

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.480
The three of them better not be off
eating something yummy.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.980
I'm starving.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.390
Hey.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.630
Is your wrist okay?

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.100
I'm not that fragile.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.440
True, you seem pretty insensitive.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.170
Did you come here to pick a fight?

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.040
I was worried about you.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.340
Worried? You?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.180
I'm telling you.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.250
I'd have beaten those guys on my own.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.220
But you just had to show off and
fight them by yourself.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.660
I'm not gonna let a girl fight.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.830
Allowing that would be
a matter of family dignity.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.330
Our honor would be harmed.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.500
What're you talking about?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.100
Nothing.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.050
Th-Thank you for yesterday!

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.240
- Huh?
- I forgot to tell you.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.760
That's all!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.160
What's up with her?

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.100
She's such a weird girl.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.670
Do you know her?

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.030
Nope.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.170
Reiji.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.210
Hey, what took you so long?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.840
Who was that just now?

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.440
Just now?

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.750
Ah, that was...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.110
Darn, I don't even know her name.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.250
Oh, come on. Spill it out.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.820
My bottom feels all itchy again.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.690
I feel bad for you.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.860
Surely, it must be hemorrhoids.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.830
No it's not!

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.680
You're late, Aila.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.450
I'm deeply sorry.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.190
What a crowd...

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.430
It's not just this arena.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.960
Gunpla fans around the world
are watching the live broadcast.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.140
Thank you for waiting.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:21.180
We'll now explain the third period
of the World Tournament.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.110
The third period is
an Original Weapon Battle.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.850
Using only the weapons decided by lot,

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.750
<i>﻿they'll fight in one-on-one battles.</i>

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.850
By lot?

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:38.560
<i>﻿The drawn weapons will be placed in
containers set up in the battlefield.</i>

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:43.760
<i>﻿We won't know what the weapons are
until the containers are opened.</i>

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.200
<i>﻿This battle requires the skill...</i>

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:51.510
<i>﻿to instantly understand the weapon
and how to control it.</i>

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.340
Choosing weapons by lot, huh.
Interesting.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.980
What if you draw a useless weapon?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.420
Then you'd have to deal with it
using your wit and resourcefulness.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:07.520
<i>﻿Would all the fighters
please come up to the stage?</i>

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.760
Drawing lots?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.260
You've got to be kidding me.
So ridiculous.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.700
All those Gunpla...

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.870
and these Gunpla Battles, too.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:25.110
We will now begin drawing lots.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.670
Ricardo Fellini, representing Italy.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.320
Weapon number 23.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.320
Nils Nielsen, representing America.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.690
Weapon number 47.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.860
Mao Yasaka,
representing Japan's 5th Block.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.600
Weapon number 7.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.530
Aila Jyrkiainen, representing Finland.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.440
Weapon number 16.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:59.810
Meijin Kawaguchi,
PPSE's special entry.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.110
Weapon number 1.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:09.650
Sei and Reiji are up next.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.520
I hope they draw a good one.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.760
This looks fun. Let me—

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:27.940
Sei, you do it.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.240
What's up?

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.170
Just do it.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.280
Sei Iori and Reiji,
representing Japan's 3rd Block.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.180
Weapon number 44.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.480
44...

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.120
An unlucky number.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.350
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.560
All fighters have drawn.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:57.230
We'll begin the third period battles
according to the weapon numbers.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.330
Our number is 44,

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:04.200
so our opponent is
the fighter with number 43.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.470
He's the one.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.240
Mr. Luang Dallara.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.820
He instantly saw the weak point of
the Star Build Strike's Absorb Shield.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.350
He's a World Tournament veteran.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.220
The guy from that time!

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:23.520
Huh?

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.330
Mr. Sei, Mr. Reiji,

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.840
I've been watching you guys closely!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:40.410
Creative ideas,
the skill to give them form,

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.280
and great control sense.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.410
Really impressive.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.720
Let's battle it out
so that we leave no regrets.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.350
Y-Yes, let's do it.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.790
- But, hey.
- ﻿Eh?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.090
It's us who're going to win.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.970
That's the spirit.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:09.300
I want to fight you at your best.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.110
Sei Iori and Reiji...

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.810
You're about to be utterly defeated.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.780
By my perfect plan,

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.490
and Mr. Luang's hidden talent.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.590
We now begin match one
of the third period.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.400
- ﻿I see the container.
- I'll retrieve it.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.110
Tonfas, huh.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.750
<i>﻿With this railgun,
even the Meijin will...!</i>

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.540
<i>﻿Whatever great weapon you have,</i>

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.910
it's pointless if you can't use it.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.710
A spray gun...

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.280
<i>﻿Bad luck!</i>

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:49.500
The rules never said you couldn't
take your opponent's weapon.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.110
<i>﻿Aila, the shield won't hold any longer.</i>

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:00.780
<i>﻿Aila!</i>

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.960
What!?

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.170
I won.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.910
Gotcha!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:38.590
Sorry.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.530
<i>﻿Thanks for waiting.</i>

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:58.940
Fellini! With this Wodom,
I'll finish you off at last.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.740
<i>﻿It's tiny!</i>

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:06.780
I feel bad for you.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.520
<i>﻿Those scissors wont cut
through this Wodom!</i>

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.790
Easy-peasy.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:25.470
<i>﻿You're using the scissors
the wrong way!</i>

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:32.040
It's Iori's and Reiji's turn next.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:37.540
Their opponent is Luang Dallara,
the Thai champion.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.280
Is he strong?

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:46.650
He's like Char Aznable,
Johnny Ridden, or Anavel Gato.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:49.220
What does that mean?

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:53.860
It means his abilities are
in the ace pilot class.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.530
- Let's go, Reiji.
- ﻿Heck yeah.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.170
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.840
- Star Build Strike.
- ﻿Here we come!

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.510
Abigorbine, go!

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.250
What's this?

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:23.190
A ﻿glove and balls?

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.290
How are we supposed to
fight with these?

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:31.530
I mean, are these even weapons?

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.340
This is just so funny.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:39.070
A glove and balls!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:40.640
So what are they for?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:45.680
To give them a dramatic defeat, of course.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:49.750
Wh-What?

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.150
No way...

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:09.270
A baseball stadium.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.010
Baseball...?

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.880
<i>﻿Announcing a change of player
for the Thai team.</i>

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:24.720
<i>﻿Pinch hitter, 3rd base 4th.
Luang Dallara, number 43.</i>

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:29.790
Looks like this match will be
more exciting than expected.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:35.360
Are you seriously going to
make Gunpla play baseball?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.030
<i>﻿Sei, what's baseball?</i>

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:39.270
You don't know?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.870
<i>I-I know what it is!</i>

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:44.910
<i>﻿We hit that thing with this, right?</i>

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.470
<i>﻿No!</i>

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:51.010
If it's baseball, Sei and Reiji
will have an advantage.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.710
Why is that?

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:57.220
﻿The batting average of even
the greatest batter is merely 30%.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:01.290
Meaning that the pitcher has
a 70% chance of winning.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:06.490
Plus, this is their first contest
and their pitching style is unknown.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.900
I wouldn't be so sure of that.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:13.830
Reiji, in baseball, you throw
the ball over that plate—

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.800
<i>﻿Play ball!</i>

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:16.740
Already!?

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:20.870
Alright, let's do this.
Take... this!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.590
<i>﻿Please watch out for foul balls.</i>

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.160
He hit it back!

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.260
What a slugger...

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.670
That swing speed...

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:48.130
Wow, he's incredible!

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:52.240
Luang Dallara was a member of
the Thai national baseball team.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.640
He was even scouted
by the major leagues.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.710
His lifetime batting average was 89.9%.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.650
Wow, it's just like a manga!

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.320
But why a foul ball?

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:08.790
With his ability,
he could easily have hit a home run.

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.930
I know you can do better than that.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.700
I want you to give your all next time!

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:23.540
Reiji, don't aim for the batter.

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:27.040
Then how about this!?

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.080
Not good enough!

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:36.850
<i>﻿I'm sorry, but I think
I've overestimated you two.</i>

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.520
I'm disappointed!

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:43.190
Reiji!

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.730
- What!?
- Iori's Gunpla...!

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.800
He caught it!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:18:00.370
No, the ball vanished,
so that didn't count.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:04.740
But with the final ball,
their Gunpla will...

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.750
be completely pulverized.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.550
The left arm is severely damaged.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.360
The joints are under
a lot of strain, too. Reiji!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.660
What's wrong with your wrist!?

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.760
It's all swollen!

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.530
When did you hurt yourself?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:28.500
It's nothing.
I tell you, I'm alright.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.540
Reiji, give me control.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.240
- ﻿No, I'll do it.
- ﻿But...!

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.080
Please let me do this!

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.810
I'm not giving up
on such a fun battle.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.780
I can take one more.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:46.090
Let me, Sei.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:51.790
Alright. But move the machine
exactly how I say.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.790
Are you going to use that
here and now?

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.300
That's our only way to win.

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:02.700
Activating RG System!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:10.540
In its current state, the output
will only be around 30%.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.210
But if I concentrate it
all on the right arm...

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:22.660
- The Star Build Strike is...
- It's glowing.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.760
That light...

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:29.760
Yes, I wanted to fight you
when you meant business!

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.200
Come, bring it!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.950
Reiji, bend the torso backwards.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.590
Lift up the left leg.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.130
Then slam it down on the ground!

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:16.110
This is it!

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.350
This is the ball!

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.170
<i>﻿Game set!</i>

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:52.250
Sei and Reiji won!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.810
Y﻿eah!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.720
Whoa, did he lose?
Are you kidding me?

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.660
Why won't you say anything?

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.330
We did it, Reiji!

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:09.100
That was a piece of cake.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.730
Mr. Sei, Mr. Reiji.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:15.340
What an incredible match that was.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:20.540
Should we face each other
again in the future, come full-on.

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.940
Mr. Luang... Yes!

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:27.010
But we'll win next time, too.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:31.780
It won't be that easy!

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:37.260
Whoa, whoa.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:41.630
They're smiling away.
What's going on?

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:46.730
I said, why won't you say anything!?

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:26.630
My head hurts.

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:28.770
I need to get out of this.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:34.970
I need to go back to my room
and get some rest.

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:37.340
That was really fun, Sei.

00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:41.610
Gunpla Battle is great, isn't it?

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.480
Yeah, I agree.

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:45.350
What do you think
our next opponent will be like?

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:47.820
Before all that, you gotta
get to the nurse's office.

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.490
I know.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.920
Who's interfering
with our battle again!?

00:23:57.920 --> 00:23:59.790
We're going to be
dragged into the water!

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.750
Next episode, "Codename: C".

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:05.000
Are we being chased by Zeon's ghost?
